Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Extend driver guide: detection sources, driver method,
 docs, real-PC protocol

- Section 3.6: split every driver into a hardware half and a system half behind
  a small access interface, so the logic is host-testable (same pattern as the
  PCI backend).
- Section 4.5: where each piece of hardware information comes from (BootInfo,
  CPUID, ACPI, SMBIOS, USB, I2C) and how to verify detection against a Linux
  live reference.
- Section 11: documentation sources (specs, BSD/Linux reference drivers, GPU
  docs, seL4), links collected by search.
- Section 12: protocol for the first run on a physical PC, based on seL4's x86
  documentation and a community report of a silent boot failure.
- Correct the storage driver crate description: it is a non-compiling mock-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
